IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s388-domestication`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`
IMPORT `dg11-s389-temporary-transfer`

-- Tests of dg11-s389-temporary-transfer.l4 (section 389). Expected values are worked by hand from the text of the section and written beside each assertion.

§ `Section 389(a) - definitions`

-- (a)(1): each event on the list a. to i. is an emergency condition. The second argument (the governing law permits a transfer on account of the event) matters only for item j.
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `war or other armed conflict` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `revolution or insurrection` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `invasion or occupation by foreign military forces` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `rioting or civil commotion of an extended nature` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `domination by a foreign power` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `expropriation, nationalization or confiscation of a material part of the assets or property of the non-United States entity` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `impairment of the institution of private property, including private property held abroad` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `the taking of any action under the laws of the United States whereby persons resident in the jurisdiction might be treated as enemies or otherwise restricted under laws of the United States relating to trading with enemies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `the immediate threat of any of the foregoing` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- item j.: another event, but only if the governing law permits the entity to transfer its domicile on account of it
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the list is "not limited to": an event it does not list is not shown NOT to be an emergency condition, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `another event that s 389(a)(1) does not list` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `another event that s 389(a)(1) does not list` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(2): the meanings of section 388(a)
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(2) the place is a foreign jurisdiction as § 388(a) defines it` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(a)(2) the place is a foreign jurisdiction as § 388(a) defines it` `another jurisdiction of the United States`
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity as § 388(a) defines it` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity as § 388(a) defines it` `a limited liability company` `this State`
-- (a)(3): trustees, managers, partners and persons performing equivalent functions count as officers and directors
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 389(b)`

-- Arguments: kind of entity; where formed; has complied with the section?; the governing law expressly prohibits the transfer?
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` `a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` `a limited liability company` `this State` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State` `a natural person` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE FALSE
-- "domicile" refers in addition to the seat, siege social, principal place of business and central administration, or an equivalent
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the domicile of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the seat of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the siege social of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the principal place of business of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the central administration of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `another equivalent of the seat under applicable law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `a place of another kind that s 389(b) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 389(c) - the submission`

-- A transfer proposed for 1 July 2026: 30 days before is 1 June 2026 ("at least 30 days prior": exactly 30 days is in time).
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the least time before the proposed transfer for the submission` EQUALS `period in days` 30
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` (YMD 2026 6 2) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE
-- the Secretary of State may have waived the 30-day period
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` (YMD 2026 6 2) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE

-- By position: copy of certificate of incorporation and bylaws, certified; certificate of existence; list of officers and directors with evidence and agreements; the (c)(4) certificate; the fee paid (dollars).
`submitted: everything, with the fee` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 10_000
`submitted: everything, fee a cent short` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 9_999.99
`submitted: everything, fee more than the fee` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 12_000
`submitted: without the certified copy` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 10_000
`submitted: without the certificate of existence` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 10_000
`submitted: without the list of officers and directors` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 10_000
`submitted: without the (c)(4) certificate` MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 10_000

-- By position: a. registered agent; b. description of the business; c. duly authorized, no violation; d. list of persons authorized to sign; e. affirmance not prohibited; f. undertaking.
`a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking a.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking b.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking c.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking d.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking e.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a (c)(4) certificate lacking f.` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

-- (c)(5): the examination fee is $10,000 under § 391(a)(20); that sum or more pays it
#ASSERT `s 389(c)(5) the examination fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid` `submitted: everything, with the fee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c)(5) the examination fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid` `submitted: everything, fee a cent short`
#ASSERT `s 389(c)(5) the examination fee prescribed under § 391 has been paid` `submitted: everything, fee more than the fee`

-- the translation: needed for any document not in English, unless waived. Arguments: any document not in English?; a translation under oath attached?; waived?
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- Arguments: what was submitted; what the (c)(4) certificate sets forth; the translation requirement is met?
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, fee more than the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, fee a cent short` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: without the certified copy` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: without the certificate of existence` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: without the list of officers and directors` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: without the (c)(4) certificate` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking a.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking b.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking c.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking d.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking e.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate lacking f.` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` `submitted: everything, with the fee` `a (c)(4) certificate setting forth a. to f.` FALSE

-- the Secretary of State's side: must notify acceptance if the documents satisfy the section and the name meets § 102(a)(1)
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State must notify the entity that the documents have been accepted for filing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State must notify the entity that the documents have been accepted for filing` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State must notify the entity that the documents have been accepted for filing` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the name of the entity is on the Secretary of State's reserved list` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the name of the entity is on the Secretary of State's reserved list` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the name of the entity is on the Secretary of State's reserved list` FALSE TRUE
-- public inspection: not available until, and unless, the entity effects a transfer
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the document submitted is available for public inspection pursuant to Chapter 100 of Title 29` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the document submitted is available for public inspection pursuant to Chapter 100 of Title 29` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the waiver: on request, supported by facts that justify it
#ASSERT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) the Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 389(d) - the annual certificate`

#ASSERT `s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` `prior to the transfer of its domicile` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` `during the transfer of its domicile` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it desires to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it does not desire to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the last day for filing the annual certificate in the year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- By position: executed by an appropriate officer or director; certifies the documents remain in effect or attaches amendments; the filing fee paid (dollars, § 391(a)(21): $2,500).
`an annual certificate in order` MEANS `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` OF TRUE, TRUE, 2_500
`an annual certificate a cent short` MEANS `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` OF TRUE, TRUE, 2_499.99
`an annual certificate not executed` MEANS `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` OF FALSE, TRUE, 2_500
`an annual certificate that certifies nothing` MEANS `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` OF TRUE, FALSE, 2_500
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` `an annual certificate in order`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` `an annual certificate a cent short`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` `an annual certificate not executed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` `an annual certificate that certifies nothing`
-- null and void on March 2 of the year if the certificate was not filed on or before March 1. Arguments: year; date the certificate was filed (if it was); the date asked about.
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 (JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)) (YMD 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 (JUST (YMD 2026 2 15)) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` 2026 (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) (YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) a proposed transfer is subject to all of the required submissions and the examination fee of subsection (c)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) a proposed transfer is subject to all of the required submissions and the examination fee of subsection (c)` FALSE

§ `Section 389(e) - making the transfer`

-- Arguments: documents accepted?; a written communication addressed to the Secretary of State?; signed by one of the persons on the (c)(4)d. list?; confirms the (c)(4) statements?; by ordinary means?;
-- emergency conditions have affected ordinary means?; the date of the communication; the date a signed duplicate was received (if it was).
#ASSERT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
-- by telegram, telex, telecopy or other writing, with emergency conditions affecting ordinary means: the signed duplicate within 30 days (1 July + 30 days = 31 July)
#ASSERT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 31))
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 8 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING
-- the other means are not open if emergency conditions have not affected the ordinary means
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 5))
#ASSERT `s 389(e) the records of the Secretary of State must reflect the transfer` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the records of the Secretary of State must reflect the transfer` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(e) the Secretary of State must certify that the entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the Secretary of State must certify that the entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(e) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer of the domicile into this State` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer of the domicile into this State` FALSE

§ `Section 389(f), (g), (h)`

-- (f): after the transfer the entity has the powers it had, except to the extent the laws of this State expressly prohibit
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the entity has the power that it had immediately prior to the transfer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the entity has the power that it had immediately prior to the transfer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the entity has the power that it had immediately prior to the transfer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the person may manage the business and affairs of the entity in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the person may manage the business and affairs of the entity in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the person may manage the business and affairs of the entity in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the activity is deemed to be doing business within this State for purposes of § 371` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the activity is deemed to be doing business within this State for purposes of § 371` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the version of the law to which a reference in this section is a reference` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the law as in effect immediately prior to the transfer of domicile`
#ASSERT `s 389(f) the version of the law to which a reference in this section is a reference` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (g): the enemy rule applies in an action in the courts of this State, to an entity that has the certificate
#ASSERT `s 389(g) the entity is deemed to be an enemy person or entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(g) the entity is deemed to be an enemy person or entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(g) the entity is deemed to be an enemy person or entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (h)
#ASSERT `s 389(h) the transfer leaves the obligation or liability unaffected` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(h) the transfer leaves the obligation or liability unaffected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 389(i), (j), (k)`

-- (i): withhold only if all four hold (the entity has transferred; the amount is a dividend or distribution to a holder of equity interests; the directors determine the holder will not have the full benefit; provision for escrow or similar is made)
#ASSERT `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- (j)
#ASSERT `s 389(j) process, orders, rules and notices may be served on the entity pursuant to § 321 as if it were a corporation of this State` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(j) process, orders, rules and notices may be served on the entity pursuant to § 321 as if it were a corporation of this State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(j) the director has done what the section requires before taking office` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(j) the director has done what the section requires before taking office` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(j) the director has done what the section requires before taking office` FALSE TRUE
-- (k): by position: resolution of the directors; certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official; agreement on service of process; appointment of the Secretary of State as agent; the address
`an application to withdraw with everything` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`an application to withdraw without the resolution` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`an application to withdraw without the diplomatic certificate` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`an application to withdraw without the service agreement` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an application to withdraw without the appointment` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`an application to withdraw without the address` MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw with everything`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw without the resolution`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw without the diplomatic certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw without the service agreement`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw without the appointment`
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` `an application to withdraw without the address`
#ASSERT `s 389(k) the Secretary of State must file the application to withdraw` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the Secretary of State must file the application to withdraw` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the Secretary of State must file the application to withdraw` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(k) the domicile of the entity has ceased to be in this State` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the domicile of the entity has ceased to be in this State` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) the domicile of the entity has ceased to be in this State` FALSE TRUE
